(instances (project "esp32dif" (path "/b3e603d3-e333-4001-bdd7-0d9678e5b92f" (reference "#PWR20") (unit 1)))))
(text "Notes\n1. Modules as wired today (README > Wiring). No PCB yet; S/PDIF input switch not included.\n2. Digi+ makes its own 3.3 V from 5V: only 5V (pins 2, 4) is connected. HAT 3V3 (pins 1, 17) stays open, so the two regulators never meet.\n3. R1/R2 2.2k pull-ups are required: the HAT expects the Pi's 1.8k. ESP32 internal pull-ups (~45k) fail while I2S runs.\n4. All HAT GND pins tied to GND. The breadboard wires only pins 6 and 39; more ground returns reduce I2C errors.\n5. IR_OUT: HAT pin 37 (BCM GPIO26), per the Geekworm Digi+ wiki; check on the board. Firmware enables the GPIO10 pull-up.\n6. SPDIF_TX0: HAT pin 22 (BCM GPIO25, unused by the HAT), fed by a wire soldered on the HAT from the optical transmitter data pin. JP1 normally closed. No series resistor: the HAT's 200R before the transmitter protects TX0; an extra 1k caused decode errors. For digi spdif / decode / trimtest.\n7. I2C addresses: WM8804 0x3B, SSD1306 0x3C. Unused DevKit strapping pins (2, 3, 7, 25-28) left open.\n8. A1 has no footprint yet: needs a DevKitC-1 v1.2 footprint (two 1x16 headers) for the PCB." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 15.24 213.36 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "ad6b3ae1-b4fe-40e6-9ede-4f390d1a7044"))
